From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7921: degrade on bad CLC records instead of
 failing init

Upstream commit 9417c5818a01 ("wifi: mt76: mt7921: validate CLC firmware
records") is in 7.2.8 stable. p03 previously carried a backport of it;
this is now only the p03 delta on top.

Upstream already skips records whose idx is beyond phy->clc[] - the
case hit by the Framework Laptop 16 (MT7922, WM firmware build
20260724143402, record with idx == 3). The two remaining record checks
still abort mt7921_load_clc() with -EINVAL, which propagates through
mt7921_run_firmware() and mt7921e_mcu_init() to mt7921_init_work() and
ends in

  mt7921e 0000:05:00.0: hardware init failed

with no interface. CLC is optional regulatory metadata: the function
already returns 0 when the firmware has no CLC region at all,
__mt7921_mcu_set_clc() starts with "if (!clc) return 0", and
mt7921_regd_init() does not look at phy->clc[]. A record the driver
cannot parse should cost the records, not the adapter. So:

  - trailing bytes too short for a record header end the loop; that is
    padding at the end of the region, not corruption
  - a record whose length underflows sizeof(*clc) or overruns the
    region ends the loop, keeping the records parsed before it (this
    still forecloses the len == 0 infinite loop)

Every memory-safety property of the upstream fix is retained: no
out-of-bounds read of a record header, no out-of-bounds write to
phy->clc[], no over-long devm_kmemdup(), and no infinite loop. The
region-table checks keep upstream's fatal -EINVAL, since a bad region
table means the image itself is unusable.

Fixes: 9417c5818a01 ("wifi: mt76: mt7921: validate CLC firmware records")
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/mcu.c | 21 +++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/mcu.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/mcu.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/mcu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/mcu.c
@@ -474,19 +474,20 @@
 		goto out;
 
 	for (offset = 0; offset < len; offset += clc_len) {
-		if (len - offset < sizeof(*clc)) {
-			dev_err(mdev->dev, "Invalid CLC record\n");
-			ret = -EINVAL;
-			goto out;
-		}
+		/* trailing bytes too short for a record header: padding at the
+		 * end of the region, not an error
+		 */
+		if (len - offset < sizeof(*clc))
+			break;
 
 		clc = (const struct mt7921_clc *)(clc_base + offset);
 		clc_len = le32_to_cpu(clc->len);
-		if (clc_len < sizeof(*clc) || clc_len > len - offset) {
-			dev_err(mdev->dev, "Invalid CLC record\n");
-			ret = -EINVAL;
-			goto out;
-		}
+
+		/* stop at a record that overruns the region or cannot advance
+		 * the loop, keeping whatever was parsed before it
+		 */
+		if (clc_len < sizeof(*clc) || clc_len > len - offset)
+			break;
 
 		/* Newer firmware may add records this driver does not use yet */
 		if (clc->idx >= ARRAY_SIZE(phy->clc))
